# 16. Final Strategic Recommendation

Atlas should not rush into more platform complexity before visible learner value increases.

Recommended sequence:

1. Publish C1/C2 after manual checklist.
2. Harden graders for `contains`, `sql_resultset`, and `csv_set_equal`.
3. Execute Phase 52 operator canary kit.
4. Ramp `json_equal` if metrics are clean.
5. Add 3–5 more portfolio-grade projects.
6. Build GitHub/LinkedIn export.
7. Deploy production.
8. Onboard first private beta users.
9. Use real learner data to improve skill model and adaptive mode.
10. Prepare public launch.

Atlas is not finished, but it has crossed an important threshold: it is no longer a loose prototype. It is now a structured, audited, trust-conscious learning platform with a credible path to launch.
